#: src/engine/Features.cpp:9 src/ui/ViewPie.cpp:50
msgid "Command palette"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:10
msgid "Ctrl+Shift+P (F3 with the Blender keymap): search every action, window, command, material, brush, layer and recent file by name, and run it with Enter."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:13 src/ui/Palette.cpp:147
msgid "Mesh symmetry check"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:14
msgid "UV > Mirrored Halves > Check Mesh Symmetry and the Symmetry view mode: how far the left and right halves of the model differ, with a heat map, the worst spots and (from Blender) the off vertices selected."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:17
msgid "Texture set lock and isolate"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:18
msgid "With texture sets: Set lock keeps a stroke on the texture set (or material slot) it starts on; Isolate dims the other sets in the viewport and keeps strokes off them."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:21
msgid "Auto texture from slot names"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:22
msgid "Edit > Auto Texture from Material Slots: a library material for each material slot, guessed from its name (Skin, Jeans, Boots_Leather...), as fill layers masked to each slot."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:25 src/ui/Palette.cpp:150 src/ui/Tools010.cpp:231
msgid "Macro recorder"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:26
msgid "Edit > Record Macro: keeps the commands you run (menus, windows, scripts, Claude) to replay on another model or save as a job for 'patina run'."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:29
msgid "Patina Assistant"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:30
msgid "Window > Assistant: type what you want in plain words (\"make the creases of the skin a bit redder\") and a small model on this computer turns it into Patina commands you can look at before keeping them. Needs a model file; nothing is sent anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:34 src/ui/BlenderLayout.cpp:414
#: src/ui/ContextMenus.cpp:209 src/ui/RetopoUI.cpp:590 src/ui/RetopoUI.cpp:760
#: src/ui/RetopoUI.cpp:761
msgid "Retopology"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:35
msgid "Retopology menu: clean quads over a high-poly model that follow its shape, at the density you set in quads per square meter. Zone lines become edge loops and split the model into zones with a resolution of their own; flow strokes set which way the quads run; a density brush fine-tunes. The quads can be exported, sent to Blender or made the model you paint, with the high-poly baked onto it."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:40
msgid "Drag and drop into the layer stack"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:41
msgid "Materials, smart materials and smart masks drag from the Materials panel onto a layer (a fill layer takes the material, a layer takes the smart mask) or between layers (a new fill layer, the smart material, there); a fill layer's material and a layer's mask drag onto other layers; Ctrl+drag copies a layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:45
msgid "More procedural materials and masks"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:46
msgid "The material editor names each generator's settings (dropdowns for its styles) and adds grime, worn edges and warp to every procedural material; the mask stack gains Pattern (any material as a mask), Grow / shrink and Edges; the Gradient and Drips smart masks; and cells, cracks, ridges and streaks for noise."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:50 src/ui/Panels.cpp:1531
msgid "Materials in Blender"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:51
msgid "Blender Link window: Add Patina's materials to Blender puts the whole material library in Blender's Asset Browser (with the Patina Bridge add-on 0.8)."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:54
msgid "Opacity, sheen, clearcoat and subsurface"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:55
msgid "Four more material properties, painted like the others: opacity (lace, nets, leaves, cut-outs), sheen (velvet), clearcoat (car paint, lacquer) and subsurface (skin, wax). Materials, brushes, layers and the base material get them; the viewport shows them; exports and Blender get their maps when they are used."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:59
msgid "Mesh check and fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:60
msgid "Mesh > Check Mesh: what the model is made of and what is wrong with it (holes, non-manifold edges, flipped faces, open seams, specks...), a heat map in the viewport, and fixes that keep the paint."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:63
msgid "Export the model, send it to Blender"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:64
msgid "File > Export Model: the model with its textures as .glb, .gltf or .obj. Blender > Send Model to Blender: the model as it is in Patina (mended...) becomes a Blender object with its textures (add-on 0.9)."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:67
msgid "Reduce polygons and levels of detail"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:68
msgid "Mesh > Reduce Polygons: fewer triangles, keeping the UV layout (the textures fit as they are), seams, material borders and open borders; Export Model can add levels of detail that share the textures."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:71
msgid "Recipes and batches"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:72
msgid "File > Batch Process: recipes (mend, reduce, transform, texture, export...) run on the open model or on whole folders of models by a hidden Patina, leaving the files as they were. Mesh > Transform too."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:75
msgid "The model's own textures and vertex colors"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:76
msgid "Opening a textured or vertex-colored model (.glb, .gltf, .obj, .fbx, .ply, or an object from Blender) brings in its materials: each material slot's textures and colors, and the vertex colors, become a paint layer, From the model, at the bottom of the stack. File > Bring In the Model's Textures does it again."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:80
msgid "Develop the textures"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:81
msgid "Adjustment layers get a photo editor's basic develop controls: temperature and tint, exposure, highlights and shadows, vibrance, and De-light, which takes the shadows baked into scanned and generated textures out. The PBR Range view shows base colors a real material would not have."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:85 src/ui/Tools030.cpp:30
msgid "Collision shapes"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:86
msgid "Mesh > Collision: boxes, a convex hull, a hull per part, or the model split into convex pieces, shown in green over the model and exported with the model (glTF, OBJ) under the names Unreal or Godot look for."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:89 src/ui/Tools030.cpp:30 src/ui/Tools035.cpp:17
msgid "Lightmap UVs"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:90
msgid "Mesh > Lightmap UVs: a second UV map for baked lighting in game engines (no overlaps, even texel density, padding for the lightmap size), saved with the project, exported in glTF and sent to Blender."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:93
msgid "Icons in the toolbars"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:94
msgid "The tools on the left and the bars over the 3D view, the UV editor and the layers show icons drawn after the ones painting and 3D programs use (brush, eraser, bucket, eyedropper, scissors...), grouped by job: paint, UV, retopology, symmetry. Resting the pointer on one shows its name and shortcut; Preferences can put the names beside the icons. Off: the names alone, as before."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:99
msgid "Right-click menus"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:100
msgid "A right-click (without dragging) opens a menu of what can be done there: in the 3D view for the spot under the pointer (pick its color, the layers painted there, fill or select its island, a note, the view), and on the tools, brushes, colors, history, notes and the empty parts of the panels."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:104
msgid "Translations"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:105
msgid "Preferences > Language: Patina in another language from a translation file (.po, the format Poedit and Weblate use) in the languages folder. Anyone can make one from the template; see the manual's Translating Patina page."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:109
msgid "Retopology preview button"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:110
msgid "A Retopology button in the bar over the 3D view shows the zones (or the density) and the quads on the model, and keeps a quick set of quads following each change, whichever panel is in front. Its arrow chooses what shows. Off: they show while the Retopology window is in front, as before."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:114
msgid "Axis gizmo"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:115
msgid "The X, Y and Z axes in the corner of the 3D view, turning with the camera, the way Blender and other 3D programs show them. Click an axis to look along it (click it again for the other side), drag to orbit."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:118
msgid "Pin and unpin in the 3D view"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:119
msgid "Pin and Unpin buttons in the bar over the 3D view for the Select and Island tools, and Alt+P to unpin there too (before, only in the UV editor). While those tools are chosen, the pinned islands show blue stripes on the model."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:123
msgid "Side views and going back"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:124
msgid "The numpad and the axis gizmo jump to the side, top and bottom views, which are orthographic until you turn away (a preference), and Numpad 0 (or the Back button under the gizmo) goes back to the view you had before. Alt while orbiting with the middle button (Shift with Alt+left) snaps the view to the nearest side view, as in Blender."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:129
msgid "View pie"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:130
msgid "Hold Z over the 3D view for a pie of eight ways to show the model: wireframe, solid, lit, path traced, unlit, seams, the UV checker and the retopology preview. Point and let go, or tap Z and click. (With More pie menus off: the 0.38 pie, with the Paint and Island tools, clear the selection and the retopology lines.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:134
msgid "Solid view"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:135
msgid "A view mode that shows the shape alone: light gray, lit by the environment, without textures or the normal map, as Blender's Solid shading."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:138
msgid "Path traced view and renders"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:139
msgid "The Path traced view mode and render images: real shadows, reflections and light bouncing between the model's parts, lit by the environment (Shift + right drag turns it), a shadow on the ground. The picture gets cleaner the longer nothing changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:143
msgid "More pie menus"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:144
msgid "Besides the view pie on Z: Shift+Z for the channels (base color, normal, roughness...), ` (the key under Esc) for the edit modes (the tools), and Q for Quick Favorites, eight items of your own. Right-click a toolbar button or a pie item to add it; Preferences > Pie menus lists them."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:148
msgid "Brush flow, hardness and angle keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:149
msgid "With the Blender keymap, G and Shift+G set the brush's flow and hardness by moving the mouse, and Ctrl+F its angle, the way F and Shift+F set its size and opacity. Click to keep the new value, right-click to go back."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:152
msgid "Baked maps as layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:153
msgid "The baked ambient occlusion, curvature and thickness each get a layer at the bottom of the layer list. Paint on it to fix the bake (the eraser brings the bake back), blur, smudge or clone it, and add levels, blur and other adjustments. Smart masks, the 3D view and exports use the fixed map."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:157
msgid "Type values into sliders"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:158
msgid "Right-click any slider to type its value: Enter keeps it, Esc goes back. A typed value stays in the slider's range. (Ctrl+click does the same.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:161
msgid "Island brush along the surface"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:162
msgid "The Island brush's Screen and Surface buttons. Surface takes the faces within the brush's size along the surface from the cursor, never a layer behind or a part only near in space. Off: the circle on screen only. Either way, faces turned away from you are left out."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:166
msgid "Select only what the camera sees"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:167
msgid "The Select tool's Visible only: a click or drag on a UV island takes just its faces the camera sees (turned toward you, on screen, not hidden behind other faces), so the inside of a model or a skin under clothes stays out."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:171
msgid "Blender: reopen an object's project"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:172
msgid "When Blender sends an object Patina doesn't have open (after a restart), Patina opens the saved project it was painted in and keeps its layers (reprojected if the mesh changed). Off: a new project each time."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:175
msgid "Blender: start from Blender's materials"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:176
msgid "An object from Blender with no project of its own starts from the textures and colors its materials show (Patina's own after a push, or any other), as a layer. Needs the Patina Bridge add-on 0.13."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:179
msgid "Guided layout"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:180
msgid "The work in five steps along the top (Model, UVs, Bake, Paint, Export), each a screen with what it needs in front, and the Guided / Full switch at the right of the menu bar. Off: the Full layout only."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:183
msgid "Bake-down"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:184
msgid "Bake > Bake Down to a Low-Poly Model: the layers of the painted high-poly model moved onto its low-poly version (a file, or the retopology's quads), with the check view and the high-poly in the compare view. Off: Use the Quads as the Model starts the layers afresh."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:188
msgid "Objects in a scene"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:189
msgid "Several models in one project, each an object with its own layers (a body, its clothes, eyes, hair): the Objects list above the layers, File > Add a Model to the Scene, a file with several meshes opened as an object each, the Object tool to move, turn and scale them, and several objects sent from Blender. Off: one model per project, a file's meshes opened as one."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:194
msgid "Move, turn and scale objects with G, R and S"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:195
msgid "In the Object tool, G moves the object with the mouse, R turns it about the line of sight and S scales it evenly, as in Blender: X, Y or Z keeps to one axis, a typed number sets the amount, Ctrl snaps, a click or Enter keeps it and a right-click or Esc puts it back. The keys are in the keymap. Off: the gizmo only."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:199 src/ui/Palette.cpp:139
msgid "Face sets"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/Features.cpp:200
msgid "Named, colored groups of faces kept in the project (the Face Sets panel): select, hide, show only one set's faces, fill or mask with one, Lock Face Sets keeps strokes inside one, the Face sets view shows them, and Blender's sculpt face sets come in with the model. Off: no panel, the lock and the view are gone."
msgstr ""

